    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0757" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/2511</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Umansky</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-13">May 13, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm receipt of
                    your note of May 5<anchor n="50" xml:id="d709-f1"/> informing me of the definite
                    character of all requisitions relating to articles and materials purchased for
                    exportation to the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics and taken over by the
                    Government of the United States between October 10, 1940 and May 1, 1941, and by
                    which you further inform me of the procedure of compensation due the owners of
                    these articles and materials.</p>
                <p>I did not fail to bring the contents of your note and its enclosures to the
                    immediate attention of my Government and of the interested Soviet economic
                    agencies.</p>
                <p>I do of course reserve the right of my Government and its economic agencies to
                    present in due time to the Government of the United States claims for full
                    compensation for all damage caused them by the abovementioned requisitions.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oumansky</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
